From 7474835fe8a89d3a4f17dfbf7d1ae07b4aa095a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Facundo Karanik <facundo.karanik@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 16:20:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7615: skip MT_TXD5_TX_STATUS_HOST for group
 frames

mt7615_mac_write_txwi() requests a host TX status for every frame except
beacons. On MT7663, a group addressed frame with this request can stay
in the firmware or hardware queue if it is held for the next DTIM when
the last power-saving station goes away. Later group frames then do not
complete, and the interface stops group traffic because of airtime queue
limit debt. The stall does not occur on MT7663E without the request.

Do not request a host TX status for group frames.

Fixes: f40ac0f3d3c0 ("mt76: mt7615: introduce mt7663e support")
Signed-off-by: Facundo Karanik <facundo.karanik@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/CAHNRTq83iAAFyYNB5D0eg3HJggJNq3xjO8Z1zi9=+yGe4uy_Lw@mail.gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7615/mac.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7615/mac.c b/mt7615/mac.c
index 76fbb780..744a053a 100644
--- a/mt7615/mac.c
+++ b/mt7615/mac.c
@@ -825,7 +825,9 @@ int mt7615_mac_write_txwi(struct mt7615_dev *dev, __le32 *txwi,
 	if (!ieee80211_is_beacon(fc)) {
 		struct ieee80211_hw *hw = mt76_hw(dev);
 
-		val = MT_TXD5_TX_STATUS_HOST | FIELD_PREP(MT_TXD5_PID, pid);
+		val = FIELD_PREP(MT_TXD5_PID, pid);
+		if (!multicast)
+			val |= MT_TXD5_TX_STATUS_HOST;
 		if (!ieee80211_hw_check(hw, SUPPORTS_PS))
 			val |= MT_TXD5_SW_POWER_MGMT;
 		txwi[5] = cpu_to_le32(val);
